Description: End or continue a tag name according to the template that follows
 A template character used to be appended to whatever tag name was being
 read, so "<div{{ attributes }}>" had the tag name "div{{" and "<{{ tag }}>"
 was not a tag at all. Now:
 - "<" followed by a print template opens a tag whose name is that print;
 - a tag or comment template, or a print marked with the "attributes" role,
   ends the tag name and is read again as the start of the attribute list;
 - any other print continues a compound name such as "h{{ level }}".
 The open tag start token carries its parts when the name holds a template,
 and the tree constructor takes the element name from those parts, keeping
 template text verbatim and lower-casing only the HTML around it.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
